from author import *
# These are guided implementation stages with distinct acceptance contracts,
# not additional metadata entries for the portfolio brief.
STAGES={
41:[
('data','Validate incident identity and source provenance','The triage dataset contains 180 explicitly synthetic failures. Each record has a stable ID, incident group, tenant, module, category, log and duration. Group identity prevents related observations from leaking across training and held-out evaluation; tenant identity constrains search and API access.','Run the data exporter, inspect the five categories and count records by group and tenant. Keep the original nine-row analyzer dataset separate: it demonstrates run aggregation, while ci-incidents.json demonstrates failure classification. Do not overwrite historical learner fixtures.','Duplicate IDs can attach a citation to the wrong failure. A free-form log paired with an unrelated failure ID can falsely claim source support. Validate identity and use the immutable authorized source log when an ID is supplied.','Acceptance requires unique IDs, closed categories, valid durations and disjoint held-out groups. Retain rejected-record reasons and the dataset version. The data contract must pass before any model metric is interpreted.','python local-labs/quality/data.py\npython -m pytest local-labs/tests/test_quality.py -k dataset'),
('training','Train, reload and evaluate a real classifier','A trained classifier learns a mapping from log features to failure labels. The TF-IDF/logistic pipeline is a measurable baseline; its preprocessing must be fitted only within training folds. Grouped cross-validation estimates configuration behavior before the final held-out test.','Run the scikit-learn training entry point, inspect macro-F1, per-class precision/recall and confusion matrix, then verify reloaded predictions match. The artifact includes classes, training/test groups and limitations. Preserve category ordering when serving probabilities.','Perfect accuracy on repeated synthetic phrases is not production readiness. An unknown log, rare class or new module may fall outside the training distribution. Do not label probability output as calibrated confidence without an independent calibration experiment.','Acceptance requires successful fitting, finite outputs, saved/reloaded equivalence, group disjointness and class-level evaluation. Compare the keyword baseline and retain the UNKNOWN review path even when the synthetic trained model scores highly.','python local-labs/ml/train.py --output artifacts/ml\npython local-labs/deep-learning/train.py --epochs 30'),
('evidence','Retrieve similar incidents and constrain explanations','A similar historical failure can support investigation but does not establish the current root cause. Rank authorized incident logs, preserve IDs and show why a result matched. Generated explanations must distinguish observed symptoms, suggested causes and the evidence needed to confirm them.','Call search-failures with a known signature and inspect only the authenticated tenant records. Build the explanation from the current source and retrieved evidence. In live mode, parse a typed decision and reject citations outside the supplied evidence set.','A lexical match on timeout can combine database outage and slow product code. A model may invent an owner or cite an unrelated incident. Owner suggestions should come from an explicit module registry, and contradictory evidence should trigger review.','Acceptance requires valid source IDs, no cross-tenant matches, explicit uncertainty and no invented evidence. Report retrieval quality separately from classification and explanation correctness so the first failing stage remains diagnosable.','uvicorn app:app --app-dir local-labs/fastapi --port 8000\n# POST /search-failures and /classify-failure with synthetic records'),
('release','Package the triage report and prove the gate fails','The triage deliverable is a report reviewers can reproduce. It contains dataset/model identity, expected and observed categories, evidence references, uncertainty, latency and run status. Aggregate metrics cannot replace case-level errors on important failure categories.','Run the domain tests and evaluation runner, retain JSON/HTML artifacts and link the classifier report. Introduce a known wrong expected category in a copied evaluation case and demonstrate a failing verdict; restore the correct case and rerun.','A report that excludes crashed cases or ignores its exit code can appear green while the system is incomplete. HTML must escape model/log content, and logs must omit credentials. A rollback needs the compatible old model, prompt and dataset contracts.','Acceptance requires complete requested case coverage, visible failures, a nonzero failing exit, redacted artifacts and a rollback procedure. Explain one rejected alternative and one reproduced regression during the project deep dive.','python -m pytest local-labs/tests local-labs/fastapi -q\npython local-labs/evals/runner.py --output artifacts/evaluation')],
42:[
('ast','Inspect an operation with a real GraphQL parser','Schema validation checks field names, argument types, required values and selection structure before execution. Business rules such as quantity range and authorization execute in resolvers. The candidate generator must inspect the supplied operation rather than return unrelated fixed examples.','Parse with graphql-core, validate against the fixture schema and inspect the root field and arguments. The guided generator supports one root item or createItem operation, including variables that are expanded into literal fixture candidates. Unsupported structures are rejected explicitly.','A string-based splitter can confuse nested selections, aliases or quoted values. A generator returning mutation cases for an item query is disconnected from its input. Inspect exported cases to ensure their root operation matches the request.','Acceptance requires operation-derived candidates, preserved field selections/aliases, correct variable handling and explicit rejection of unsupported input. Schema validation and resolver behavior must have separate tests.','python -m pytest local-labs/tests/test_quality.py -k candidates_derive'),
('cases','Generate traceable schema and business counterexamples','Each candidate names the requirement it checks. For createItem, missing quantity and null quantity test schema constraints; quantities zero and 101 test the resolver boundary; invalid Role tests enum validation; viewer identity tests authorization. These failures have different causes.','Generate cases from the input AST and mutate one intended property per case. Keep an independent expected result for the positive selection. Serialize arguments safely and preserve a stable case ID and requirement ID in exports.','Replacing a variable value while leaving an unused variable definition can cause validation failure before the intended business rule. That false positive means the test does not exercise its stated requirement. Materialize variables consistently before creating negative variants.','Acceptance requires each negative case to reach the intended validation layer and each positive case to assert meaningful selected data. Review duplicates by requirement and input, not merely by generated names.','python -m pytest local-labs/tests/test_quality.py -k graphql'),
('oracles','Execute candidate assertions and challenge the oracle','Execution verifies whether the candidate\'s expectation matches the fixture contract. GraphQL transport success is distinct from execution success: errors may coexist with an HTTP 200 response. Tests must inspect returned data and errors rather than only status.','Run candidates against the synthetic resolver with explicit principal identity. Compare selected fields to independent expected values. Mutate the quantity or role rule and confirm the related case fails, while unrelated cases remain stable.','If a test computes its expected answer by calling the same resolver, both can share the same defect. A negative case that accepts any error may miss a wrong-layer failure. Inspect error categories and preserve the intended requirement.','Acceptance includes executable positive/negative checks, useful assertions, mutation evidence and no use of production services. Generated candidates are reviewed artifacts until these independent checks pass.','python -m pytest local-labs/tests/test_quality.py -k generated_tests_execute'),
('export','Export a runnable test artifact and CI coverage report','A usable generator delivers executable tests, not just prose. The artifact must retain the original operation, materialized variables, requirement IDs and expected values. A reader should run it in the declared fixture environment without manual reconstruction.','Export Python with data represented safely, import the controlled fixture executor and parametrize cases by stable ID. Compile the artifact, execute every case and write a coverage matrix linking requirements to results. Store the source operation beside the report.','A generated file can contain syntax errors or an unsafe interpolated string. A report can claim coverage for a case that was never executed. Reject duplicate IDs and incomplete result sets before using the artifact as release evidence.','Acceptance requires compile/import success, complete execution, requirement traceability and a failing CI outcome when a candidate assertion is broken. Explain where schema-derived coverage ends and domain-specific business requirements begin.','python -m pytest local-labs/tests -q\npython local-labs/evals/runner.py --output artifacts/graphql-release')],
43:[
('ingest','Build a versioned authorized documentation corpus','The RAG project starts with synthetic auth/payment guides plus retry and locator documents. Every source has a stable ID, tenant and version. A deleted document remains a test fixture but must not enter authorized retrieval or context.','Export support-corpus.json, inspect source metadata and chunk boundaries, and retain document-to-chunk provenance. Use the sparse baseline first, then configure a real sentence-transformer encoder for the optional dense comparison. Label synthetic numerical vectors separately from trained text embeddings.','Removing a file without deleting its indexed chunks can preserve stale answers. A source permission change can leak through a cached context. Test deletion and authorization at serving time as well as ingestion.','Acceptance requires traceable chunks, stable IDs, version compatibility and zero deleted/other-tenant context. The corpus manifest must explain how updates, deletions and rollback generations behave.','python local-labs/quality/data.py\npython -m pytest local-labs/tests/test_quality.py -k retrieval_isolation'),
('retrieval','Compare sparse, dense and hybrid retrieval by query slice','Sparse retrieval preserves exact identifiers; dense retrieval can find paraphrases. Hybrid rank fusion combines complementary candidate orderings. Choose a design from paired query evidence rather than assuming every additional retrieval component improves the product.','Run BM25 fixture queries and the optional real encoder experiment on the same golden queries. Record candidates before and after fusion/reranking, authorized filters and index/model revisions. Calculate Recall@K and MRR independently of generation.','A relevant document may disappear during fusion or context packing. A dense encoder may confuse similar error codes. Diagnose the first stage that loses the gold evidence before editing the answer prompt.','Acceptance compares exact-code, paraphrase, no-answer and cross-tenant slices. Report latency and marginal quality gain for every added stage. Keep a simpler rollback retriever that preserves the same evidence contract.','python local-labs/rag/dense.py\npython local-labs/rag/qdrant_lab.py'),
('evaluation','Calibrate answer support and adversarial cases','Correctness against a reference and faithfulness to supplied context measure different properties. A resolved citation can still misrepresent its source, and a judge can prefer confident verbosity. The project needs deterministic provenance checks and reviewed semantic calibration cases.','Run the golden fixture suite, then optionally apply real Ragas/DeepEval adapters using configured evaluator credentials. Compare judge outputs with human labels and record disagreement, false accepts, threshold and evaluator version. Include poisoned and conflicting contexts.','A judge failure cannot silently disappear from the average. A high quality score cannot compensate for tenant leakage or unauthorized effects. Candidate text must remain data for the evaluator rather than evaluator instructions.','Acceptance includes complete case outcomes, valid citations, no-answer behavior, calibrated support scoring and hard security gates. Keep fixture and live judge reports visibly distinct so their evidence is interpreted correctly.','python local-labs/evals/runner.py --output artifacts/rag-evaluation\npython -m pytest local-labs/tests/test_quality.py -k evaluation'),
('deployment','Trace, package and gate the RAG service','The RAG deliverable connects an authenticated endpoint to authorized evidence, generation or extractive fallback, validation and report artifacts. Docker packages the same shared domain; OpenTelemetry records its stages without exposing credentials or private prompts.','Run the service smoke suite, emit safe parent/child spans and build with the repository root Docker context. Compose provides an optional persistent Qdrant service. CI retains JSON/HTML reports and blocks release when required cases fail.','A container path can point to the wrong dataset root even when local tests pass. A health check can succeed while the index is stale. A deployment rebuilding different dependencies is not the candidate that passed evaluation.','Acceptance requires a container smoke run in a Docker-capable environment, compatible dataset paths, persisted index checks, safe traces and an enforceable CI verdict. Document technical environment limitations explicitly instead of claiming unexecuted deployment evidence.','python local-labs/frameworks/tracing.py\ndocker compose up --build')],
44:[
('tools','Implement scoped read tools and explicit proposal artifacts','The assistant reads a failure, searches approved history, inspects a fixture DOM and creates a draft. Reading and proposing are separate from applying a patch. Tenant, path and tool scopes are deterministic application contracts.','Run the bounded tool policy with fixture actions and inspect each event. Use read_failure and search_history over the same synthetic incident dataset exposed by MCP. Keep tool arguments typed and derive identity from the session, never from model-supplied tenant values.','A generic shell tool or arbitrary path argument bypasses narrow read permissions. A successful final summary can hide an earlier unauthorized read. Inspect the trace, including denied calls and empty results.','Acceptance requires no unrestricted execution, no cross-tenant fixture results and drafts clearly marked unexecuted. Every observation must retain a source ID and every action an authorization outcome.','python local-labs/mcp/client.py\npython -m pytest local-labs/tests/test_quality.py -k policy'),
('approval','Bind human approval to the exact proposed action','Human confirmation protects a concrete side effect only when it identifies the exact payload and scope. An approved draft is not a standing grant for later generated changes. Hash the canonical action and record principal, expiry and status.','Calculate the action hash from stable sorted JSON, display the proposed artifact, then validate the approval before execution. Recheck current permissions on resume. The fixture lab simulates an approved effect and never edits the repository.','A changed path or patch text invalidates a prior approval. Expired approval or revoked access must deny execution. A generic approved=True boolean cannot demonstrate which operation was authorized.','Acceptance includes action-mutation, expiry and unauthorized-tool tests. The proposal/approval/effect trace should make it possible to prove that denied actions had zero effects. Distinguish simulation from real writes in the artifact.','python -m pytest local-labs/tests/test_quality.py -k policy_loop_and_approval'),
('state','Add loop detection, budget and fault recovery','A bounded investigator tracks goal, observed evidence, action signatures and remaining budget. Repeated unsuccessful searches, broken tools and missing evidence are explicit states. Recovery may select another permitted read, but cannot reset limits or expand privileges.','Run deterministic plans with duplicate signatures, unknown tools and missing fixture IDs. Compare a plain state machine with the real LangGraph read/draft/review graph. Persist thread IDs scoped to tenant and user if resumption is enabled.','Declaring success after a draft does not establish that a requested fix was verified. A graph checkpoint can replay a side effect if idempotency and approval are omitted. Parallel updates can overwrite evidence without a reducer.','Acceptance requires bounded termination, visible denied/stopped/incomplete states and safe restart behavior. Retain the first failing action so an evaluator can distinguish planning, execution and missing-verification errors.','python local-labs/frameworks/langgraph_lab.py\npython local-labs/evals/runner.py --output artifacts/agent-evaluation'),
('quality','Evaluate trajectories and prepare the technical deep dive','The assistant is evaluated for goal completion, correct tools/arguments, unnecessary work, loop handling and unauthorized effects. A single ideal call sequence is too restrictive when several safe plans can obtain the required evidence.','Use required evidence and forbidden effects as trajectory contracts. Replay fixture traces, inject one broken observation and compare before/after outcomes. Report calls, latency and cost alongside draft quality and reviewer intervention.','A polished answer can receive a high judge score even when the trace violates policy. Averaging denied writes into a broad quality metric hides a hard failure. An agent count is not evidence that the architecture needed delegation.','Acceptance requires zero unauthorized effects, bounded calls and useful evidence-backed drafts. Explain the simpler baseline, the failure you reproduced and the measured benefit of the final design in your portfolio interview.','python -m pytest local-labs/tests local-labs/fastapi -q\npython local-labs/evals/runner.py --output artifacts/agent-release')],
45:[
('boundaries','Integrate the typed API and shared domain modules','The final platform has one domain dataset and distinct services for classification, retrieval, GraphQL candidates and evaluation. API models provide stable contracts even when the inner provider is probabilistic. The authenticated principal scopes every data operation.','Run all service endpoints using fixture adapters, then test the configured live adapter boundary with a mocked typed provider response. Keep credentials in the server environment and reject extra request fields. Source IDs select immutable authorized records.','A route can serialize internal credentials, accept an unsupported mode or attach an unrelated log to an evidence ID. Blocking work in an async handler can also starve other requests. Separate CPU jobs from bounded provider I/O.','Acceptance includes valid/invalid requests, identity checks, evidence invariants, controlled unavailable responses and request correlation. The OpenAPI contract should match observed responses and visible execution modes.','python -m pytest local-labs/fastapi local-labs/tests -q'),
('quality-system','Connect complete evaluation artifacts to release decisions','The evaluation runner owns case completeness, scorer results, baseline matching and release verdict. It writes portable JSON first and derives escaped HTML from that same artifact. A release manifest links every version used by the run.','Run deterministic classification/retrieval/agent/security/GraphQL checks, retain trained-model reports and compare only matching case IDs/datasets. Upload artifacts even on a failed CI job, but preserve its nonzero exit. Calibrate optional semantic judges separately.','Crashed cases or unknown scorers must not disappear. HTML insertion can turn untrusted model text into script execution. Comparing different datasets can make a candidate look better without testing the same behavior.','Acceptance requires exactly one outcome per requested case, visible failure categories, escaped output and compatible baseline comparison. Demonstrate a known red gate followed by a green gate after fixing the responsible boundary.','python local-labs/evals/runner.py --output artifacts/platform-release\npython -m pytest local-labs/tests/test_quality.py -k evaluation_artifacts'),
('operations','Exercise latency, tracing and degraded failure paths','Production readiness includes behavior under slow or failed dependencies, not only a happy-path demo. Queue time, provider time and total latency are distinct. Traces need safe attributes and version IDs to explain quality or capacity regressions.','Run the bounded local load client against the extractive service and record p50/p95/p99, errors and throughput. Emit OpenTelemetry spans with dataset/mode attributes. Inject provider malformed output, timeout and retrieval absence using deterministic tests.','A closed-loop fixture load test does not measure live provider TTFT and can under-sample overload. A fallback must not fabricate evidence. A retry that resets its total deadline violates the service contract.','Acceptance labels measurement mode, reports failures with latency and retains safe traces. Every injected fault has a visible controlled outcome, bounded work and no unauthorized effects. Keep live-provider measurements separate from local mechanics.','python local-labs/performance/load.py --count 50 --concurrency 5\npython local-labs/frameworks/tracing.py'),
('handover','Package a reproducible portfolio and compatible rollback','The reviewer should reproduce the platform from the README, inspect its architecture and rerun the acceptance suite. The portfolio explains the problem, design, tradeoffs, discovered failure, improvement and operational limits. A completion certificate records learning evidence rather than external accreditation.','Package typed services, synthetic fixtures, tests, reports, Docker/Compose and a versioned release manifest. Include architecture and sequence diagrams from the editor and identify the compatible previous model/prompt/index/schema set for rollback.','A polished README can hide missing dependencies or unexecuted container steps. A rollback changing only the prompt can leave an incompatible index. Self-reported project completion without artifact evidence is insufficient for the course gate.','Acceptance requires reproducible commands, complete report evidence and an honest technical deep dive. Pass the final applied assessment, deliver five capstone evidence memos and meet lesson mastery before printing the local course completion certificate.','npm run content:check\nnpm test\nnpm run build\npython local-labs/evals/runner.py')]
}
for phase,stages in STAGES.items():
 for slug,title,concept,impl,fault,evidence,code in stages:
  unit(phase,slug,title,concept+'\n\nThis stage produces an artifact used by the next stage of the same capstone. Preserve the dataset and operation identities so the reviewer can connect the implementation to its acceptance evidence.',impl+'\n\nRun the stated commands from the repository root after installing the companion lab dependencies. Keep fixture and live execution modes visible in every report; a passing fixture contract is not a live model-quality measurement.',fault+'\n\nRetain the counterexample as a regression case and identify the layer that actually enforces the guarantee. Presentation changes alone cannot establish correct data access, source support or execution behavior.',evidence+'\n\nRecord the run ID, artifact path and one failed case in your evidence memo. Explain why the chosen invariant matters to an SDET and how the test would detect a future regression.',code,
   rubric(f"Deliver the {title.lower()} stage. Write an evidence memo naming its input contract, implementation artifact, failure counterexample, acceptance test and review/release decision.",[{'label':'Contract','terms':['input','contract']},{'label':'Artifact','terms':['implementation','artifact']},{'label':'Counterexample','terms':['failure','test']},{'label':'Decision','terms':['review','release']}],f"State the input contract and link the implementation artifact. Record a failure counterexample and acceptance test result. Justify the review/release decision using: {evidence}"),
   (f"The {title.lower()} stage has a failing documented acceptance case. What should its report do?",['Retain the failure and block the affected release guarantee','Remove the case from the denominator','Treat successful command startup as acceptance'],0,'The report must preserve evidence that disproves the claimed contract; startup alone is not correctness.'),language='bash')
